WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.205
Women are not only 
supposed to have&nbsp;children,

00:00:04.778 --> 00:00:06.668
they are supposed to want to.

00:00:06.668 --> 00:00:12.000
This existed everywhere. It existed&nbsp;
in the ways that adults spoke to me

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.788
when they posed questions in the context of

00:00:15.788 --> 00:00:17.448
"When you get married ..."

00:00:17.448 --> 00:00:19.239
"When you have kids ..."

00:00:19.239 --> 00:00:20.748
"Don't you want a family?"

00:00:20.748 --> 00:00:24.540
A value that&nbsp;I have always understood 
about myself was that

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.751
I never wanted children.

00:00:26.751 --> 00:00:29.940
It's so easy to&nbsp;forget the roles
 that society places on us

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.793
are so much more than mere titles.

00:00:32.793 --> 00:00:34.740
What&nbsp;about the weight that comes with them,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.751
the pressure to conform to these standards

00:00:37.751 --> 00:00:39.948
... the fear associated with questioning them,

00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:42.170
and the desires that we cast 
aside to&nbsp;accept them?

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.946
Your choice to embrace or forego motherhood

00:00:44.946 --> 00:00:48.212
is not in any way tied to your&nbsp;
worthiness or identity

00:00:48.212 --> 00:00:51.335
as spouses, as adults, or as women ...

00:00:51.335 --> 00:00:55.298
and there absolutely is a 
choice&nbsp;behind maternity,

00:00:55.298 --> 00:00:58.600
and it is yours and yours alone.

